raged  Hawaii lawmakers to propose a statewide  ban on the sale of all sunscreens that  contain oxybenzone state senator will  espero says people will have to learn to  use sun blocks that contain titanium and  zinc instead if Hawaii does approve this  ban it'll be the first state to do so  yes I'd like to see Hawaii take the lead  and make certain that we can do all we  can to protect our ocean environment but  sunscreen makers are fighting back a  group representing about 90% of the  cosmetic and personal care products  industry says there is no conclusive  scientific evidence that sunscreen  ingredients negatively impact coral  reefs at levels that have been detected  in tourist areas dr. Richmond disagrees  the levels that were finding in the  water are the levels at which it's  having that biological impact what can  we do to slow down what's happening at  this point it's real tough to think  about ways to slow  ocean warming but locally we can do a  lot to take stress off the reef so  sunscreen might be a good place to start  it's one that we can all contribute to  for CBS this morning Carter Evans Kona  Hawaii really interesting story what are  we doing to the planet yeah just use  sunblock y'all yes I'm back all right
 

